    <<ad _ad>>

<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“S- sorry…”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> says as he wipes his face, still looking away from you, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I didn’t mean to ruin the party, I just… I just need a minute, I’ll be down in a second.”</span> He takes a deep breath, trying hard to keep his emotions under control, <span style="Color: LightCoral">but you can hear the quiver in his voice as it breaks and he continues to sob. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I’m sorry… You can go get some food or ask my dad to take you home… sorry our night’s ruined…”</span> You feel your own lip quiver as the boy seems more concerned about ruining your time here than what he is clearly going through.</span> Softly, you walk over and sit down next to him, putting your arm around his shoulders and asking if he’s alright. <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Y- yeah… I just… lost my head, I just need and second and I’ll…”</span> <span style="Color: LightCoral">But <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> can’t hold back his feelings as he starts to cry, trying to pull away from you out of shame and embarrassment, but you pull him closer, telling him it’s okay and patting him on the back. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“It’s… it’s just so stupid. I don’t even know why I’m upset, I just…”</span> He pauses as his voice stutters and breaks,</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I just wanted today, just today, to be about me. I know it’s selfish, but I- I don’t care about that stupid award or the ceremony! I just wanted my family… my mom to just see me! But I can’t live up to him, no matter what I do!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> takes a few deep breaths,<span style="Color: LightCoral">his crying settling but his voice still trembles and cracks.</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“It’s always <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Connor</span>. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Connor</span> getting hurt or wanting to do something else or what flavor of cake he wants for his birthday or what he wants for dinner. I just-!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> sighs, sitting in silence for a long minute, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Whenever she looks at me, she sees <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Connor</span>. She has to… because it’s the only way it all makes sense to her. It’s not her fault, but… I’m just tired…”</span> <br>
<br>

<<linkreplace"Continue">>
    <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I’m tired of everything I do somehow being about him. How we always have to be equal in her mind. I’m tired of wondering who she is talking to when she looks at me. I’m tired of seeing her get disappointed when she realizes it’s only me. I’m tired of feeling like… like I have to be both of us.”</span> <br>
    <br>
    <span style="Color: LightCoral"><span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>’s voice drops, another long pause before he whispers something he’s never said out loud.</span> <br>
    <br>
    <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I’m tired of living from someone who’s dead.”</span> <br>
    <br>
    <<linkreplace"Continue">>
        <span style="Color: LightCoral">There is a long pause where you just stare at <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>, wondering if you heard him right.</span> <span style="Color: Yellow">But as it dawns over you, it starts to make sense. Maybe this thought has crossed your mind, maybe it hasn’t. You have so many questions, but you don’t ask them. Right now, it’s about <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>.</span> <br>
        <br>
        <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I’m sorry I didn’t tell you. I wanted to, but it isn’t something I can bring up easily. Then when my mom met you at the park and mentioned him I… I didn’t want to scare you away, because I liked you.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> leans his head on you, staring blankly ahead at a small, framed photo. <span style="Color: Yellow">It’s of <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> and <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Connor</span> as toddlers, smiling.</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“<span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Connor</span>… died when we were around three. I… I don’t know all the details. I was too little to remember it really. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Callum</span> told me a little bit when I asked, but… it makes them sad when I ask… So I don’t. But I know he got sick. It was sudden and… and he didn’t make it. He didn’t come home that night… and then… something bad happened. They won’t tell me what, but I can guess.”</span> <br>

            <<set _ad to [
                {
                    Name: "Player",
                    State: {
                        Mouth: "Frown",
                        Blush: 1,
                    },
                },
                {
                    Name: "Carter",
                    State: {
                        Outfit: "Everyday",
                        Mouth: "Frown",
                        Eyes: "Tired",
                        Blush: 1,
                        Cry: 1,
                    },
                },
            ]>>
            <<ad _ad>>

        As <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> speaks, he moves closer to you. <span style="Color: Yellow">You don’t think he’s ever said this out loud, and the words sound like they hurt to speak. You tell him it’s okay, he doesn’t have to tell you.</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I… I want to…”</span> He gulps, wiping his face on his shirt. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Mom had to go away for a while, a long while. Dad said she got sick too, but like… different sick. I still saw her, sometimes, but she didn’t come back to live with us until after I started school. But she was different when she came back. She…”</span> He takes a deep breath, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“She acted like <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Connor</span> was still around. Like he was growing up next to me and stuff. Sometimes, when I’d do stuff or talk to her, she would act like I was <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Connor</span>. Since we look the same, I guess.”</span> <br>
        <br>
        <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Dad… tired to talk her out of it at first. Got her a doctor to help and some medicine to make things clearer, but… whenever she takes her medicine she gets really sad, she can’t get out of bed most of the time. I don’t like seeing her like that.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> explains, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“<span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Callum</span> said some bad things happened, so dad stopped trying. He lets her pretend that <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Connor</span>’s still here because… because he doesn’t want her to go away again. And I don’t mind it, really! I can share her with him, even if he’s not here. And when I need her, she tries, she really really tries! And I know she tried tonight and it’s not her fault she can’t, but… I thought getting an award like this… maybe she would see me as me. She would realize I’m still here… even if <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Connor</span> isn’t.”</span> <br>
        <br>
        <span style="Color: Yellow"><span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> goes quiet, just resting on you as he stares at the photo. You process all that he said, the events of the night and even other times starting to become clear. His dad’s shame, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Callum</span>’s anger at them letting this happen, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> throwing himself in the middle to show he’s okay with all of it. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> doesn’t like to see people sad, so he puts on a smile. But as you look down at him, at his red, damp face, you realize that for once he isn’t forcing a smile or pretending to be okay.</span> <span style="Color: LightCoral">He just looks tired…</span> <br>
        <br>
        <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I’m sure I made them all sad when I ran off like that. I just didn’t want to cry in front of everyone.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> says after a long silence, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Sorry, I know we were going to watch movies and eat pizza and stuff but… I don’t want to go down right now. You can go home, if you want. I’ll be fine…”</span> But you don’t leave. <span style="Color: Pink">Despite what <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> says, he doesn’t want to be alone right now. So, you tell him you’re not going anywhere.</span> <br>
        <br>
